and O
placebo O
are O
different O
in O
nature O
and O
rely O
on O
different O
neuropsychological O
mechanisms. O
We O
discuss O
possible O
explanations O
and O
their O
implications O
for O
clinical O
practice O
and O
future O
research. O

Cognitive O
control O
refers O
to O
a O
set O
of O
mental O
processes O
that O
enable O
individuals O
to O
flexibly O
and O
adaptively O
engage O
in O
goal-directed O
behavior. O
Adolescence O
is O
characterized O
by O
the O
emergence O
and O
subsequent O
rapid O
development O
of O
adult-like O
cognitive O
control O
abilities, O
and O
as O
such, O
