Traumatic O
brain O
injury O
(TBI) O
is O
highly O
prevalent O
among O
very O
young O
and O
older O
adults, O
with O
poorer O
outcomes O
and O
longer O
recovery O
in O
aged O
individuals. O
The O
brain O
is O
a O
lipid-rich O
organ O
and O
high O
rates O
of O
membrane O
remodeling O
occur O
during O
recovery, O
yet O
remain O
poorly O
delineated, O
especially O
in O
aged. O
To O
determine O
the O
impact O
of O
age O
on O
lipid O
metabolism O
during O
TBI O
recovery, O
TBI O
was O
induced O
by O
control O
cortical O
impact O
in O
3 O
(young) O
and O
20 O
(aged) O
month-old O
mice. O
The O
ipsilateral O
cortex O
was O
harvested O
at O
1-, O
3-, O
7-, O
and O
28-day O
post O
injury O
(dpi) O
for O
analysis O
of O
gene O
expression, O
membrane O
lipidomics, O
total O
lipid O
fatty O
acid O
profile, O
and O
intermediates O
of O
fatty O
acid O
β-oxidation, O
acylcarnitines. O
Lipid O
