genes O
were O
largely O
downregulated O
in O
response O
to O
TBI O
in O
young O
mice, O
yet O
remained O
unchanged O
or O
were O
increased O
in O
aged O
mice, O
resulting O
in O
significantly O
higher O
expression O
in O
aged O
compared O
to O
young. O
TBI O
increased O
acylcarnitines O
by O
a O
robust O
~3-fold O
in O
both O
young O
and O
aged O
cohorts O
acutely O
following O
injury O
and O
restored O
to O
sham O
levels O
by O
day O
28. O
Phospholipidome O
compositional O
analysis O
reveals O
largest O
changes O
in O
the O
aged O
mice O
at O
28 O
dpi. O
Aged O
mice O
phospholipid O
profiles O
shifted O
towards O
higher O
mono- O
and O
di- O
unsaturated O
and O
lower O
saturated O
and O
highly O
polyunsaturated O
species. O
Phospholipids O
with O
4 O
unsaturated O
bonds, O
predicted O
to O
contain O
arachidonic O
acid, O
tended O
to O
increase O
post-TBI, O
whereas O
species O
containing O
6 O
unsaturated O
bonds, O
predicted O
to O
contain O
docosahexaenoic O
acid O
(DHA) O
steadily O
declined O
during O
recovery. O
Total O
fatty O
acid O
analysis O
confirmed O
decreased O
DHA O
at O
28 O
dpi O
in O
aged O
mice O
and O
more O
severely O
after O
TBI. O
In O
summary, O
TBI O
in O
aged O
led O
to O
a O
loss O
of O
transcriptional O
repression, O
more O
profound O
phospholipid O
change, O
earlier O
upregulation O
of O
acylcarnitines, O
and O
significant O
