on O
lipid O
content. O

Brain O
activity O
patterns O
in O
high-level O
visual O
cortex O
support O
accurate O
linear O
classification O
of O
visual O
concepts O
(e.g., O
objects O
or O
scenes). O
It O
has O
long O
been O
appreciated O
that O
the O
accuracy O
of O
linear O
classification O
in O
any O
brain O
area O
depends O
on O
the O
geometry O
of O
its O
concept O
manifolds-sets O
of O
brain O
activity O
patterns O
that O
encode O
images O
of O
a O
concept. O
However, O
it O
is O
unclear O
how O
the O
geometry O
of O
concept O
manifolds O
differs O
between O
regions O
of O
visual O
cortex O
that O
support O
accurate O
classification O
and O
those O
that O
don't, O
or O
how O
it O
differs O
between O
visual O
cortex O
and O
deep O
neural O
networks O
(DNNs). O
We O
estimated O
geometric O
properties O
of O
concept O
manifolds O
that, O
per O
a O
recent O
theory, O
directly O
determine O
the O
accuracy O
of O
simple O
"few-shot" O
linear O
classifiers. O
Using O
a O
large O
fMRI O
dataset, O
we O
show O
that O
variation O
in O
classification O
accuracy O
across O
human O
visual O
cortex O
is O
driven O
by O
a O
variation O
in O
a O
single O
geometric O
property: O
the O
distance O
between O
manifold O
centers O
("geometric O
Signal"). O
In O
contrast, O
variation O
in O
classification O
accuracy O
across O
early O
and O
mid O
DNN O
layers O
is O
driven O
by O
an O
increase O
in O
the O
effective O
number O
of O
manifold O
dimensions O
("Dimensionality"). O
Despite O
this O
difference O
in O
the O
geometric O
properties O
that O
affect O
few-shot O
classification O
performance O
in O
the O
brain O
and O
DNNs, O
we O
find O
that O
Signal O
and O
Dimensionality O
are O
strongly, O
negatively O
correlated: O
when O
Signal O
increases O
across O
brain O
regions O
or O
DNN O
layers, O
Dimensionality O
decreases, O
and O
vice O
versa. O
We O
conclude O
that O
early O
visual O
cortical O
areas O
and O
DNN O
layers O
deploy O
different O
geometric O
strategies O
for O
accurate O
linear O
classification O
of O
concepts, O
even O
though O
both O
are O
subject O
to O
the O
same O
constraint. O

BackgroundIn O
patients O
with O
severe O
acute O
brain O
injury O
(SABI) O
admitted O
to O
the O
Intensive O
Care O
Unit O
(ICU) O
outcome O
is O
often O
