cognitive O
concerns, O
with O
no O
diagnosis O
of O
major O
psychiatric, O
neurological O
or O
systemic O
disorders O
who O
were O
recruited O
consecutively O
between O
April O
2022 O
and O
July O
2023 O
were O
included. O
Participants O
underwent O
neuropsychological O
assessments O
and O
structural O
MRI, O
and O
were O
classified O
as O
cognitively O
normal, O
with O
MCI O
or O
with O
dementia. O
MRI O
pre-processing O
using O
automated O
pipelines, O
along O
with O
human-based O
visual O
ratings, O
were O
compared O
against O
AI-based O
automated O
AQUA O
output. O
Default O
mode O
network O
grey O
matter O
(GM) O
volumes O
were O
compared O
between O
cognitively O
normal, O
MCI O
and O
dementia O
groups. O
A O
total O
of O
90 O
participants O
(mean O
age O
at O
visit O
was O
63.32±10.96 O
years) O
were O
included O
in O
the O
study O
(30 O
cognitively O
normal, O
40 O
MCI O
and O
20 O
dementia). O
Non-parametric O
Spearman O
correlation O
analysis O
indicated O
that O
AQUA-based O
and O
human-based O
visual O
ratings O
were O
correlated O
with O
total O
(ρ=0.66; O
P<0.0001), O
periventricular O
(ρ=0.50; O
P<0.0001) O
and O
deep O
(ρ=0.57; O
P<0.0001) O
white O
matter O
hyperintensities O
(WMH). O
Additionally, O
volumetric O
WMH O
obtained O
from O
AQUA O
and O
automated O
pipelines O
was O
also O
strongly O
correlated O
(ρ=0.84; O
P<0.0001) O
and O
these O
correlations O
remained O
after O
controlling O
for O
age O
at O
visit, O
sex O
and O
diagnosis. O
Linear O
regression O
analyses O
illustrated O
significantly O
different O
AQUA-derived O
default O
mode O
network O
GM O
volumes O
between O
cognitively O
normal, O
MCI O
and O
dementia O
groups. O
Dementia O
participants O
had O
significant O
atrophy O
in O
the O
posterior O
cingulate O
cortex O
compared O
to O
cognitively O
normal O
participants O
(P=0.021; O
95% O
confidence O
interval O
[CI] O
-1.25 O
to O
-0.08) O
and O
in O
the O
hippocampus B-Brain
compared O
to O
cognitively O
normal O
(P=0.0049; O
95% O
CI O
-1.05 O
to O
-0.16) O
and O
MCI O
participants O
(P=0.0036; O
95% O
CI O
-1.02 O
to O
-0.17). O
Our O
findings O
demonstrate O
high O
concordance O
between O
human-based O
visual O
ratings O
and O
AQUA-based O
ratings O
of O
WMH. O
Additionally, O
the O
AQUA O
GM O
segmentation O
pipeline O
showed O
good O
