regions O
between O
cognitively O
normal, O
MCI O
and O
dementia O
participants. O
Based O
on O
these O
findings, O
the O
automated O
AQUA O
software O
could O
aid O
clinicians O
in O
examining O
MRI O
scans O
of O
patients O
with O
cognitive O
impairment. O

Behavioral O
variant O
frontotemporal O
dementia O
(bvFTD), O
the O
most O
common O
subtype O
of O
FTD, O
is O
a O
leading O
form O
of O
early-onset O
dementia O
worldwide. O
Accurate O
and O
timely O
diagnosis O
of O
bvFTD O
is O
frequently O
delayed O
due O
to O
symptoms O
overlapping O
with O
common O
psychiatric O
disorders, O
and O
interest O
has O
increased O
in O
identifying O
biomarkers O
that O
may O
aid O
in O
differentiating O
bvFTD O
from O
psychiatric O
disorders. O
To O
summarize O
and O
critically O
review O
studies O
examining O
whether O
neurofilament O
light O
chain O
(NfL) O
in O
cerebrospinal O
fluid O
(CSF) O
or O
blood O
is O
a O
viable O
aid O
in O
the O
differential O
diagnosis O
of O
bvFTD O
vs O
psychiatric O
disorders. O
A O
systematic O
review O
was O
conducted, O
searching O
PubMed, O
Embase, O
Web O
of O
Science, O
PsycINFO, O
and O
the O
Cochrane O
Collaborative O
according O
to O
Preferred O
Reporting O
Items O
for O
a O
Systematic O
Review O
and O
Meta-Analysis O
of O
Diagnostic O
Accuracy O
Studies O
(PRISMA-DTA) O
guidelines. O
Eligible O
articles O
included O
cohorts O
of O
patients O
with O
bvFTD O
and O
psychiatric O
disorders O
ascertained O
using O
validated O
methods O
and O
conducted O
analyses O
to O
evaluate O
NfL O
from O
CSF O
and/or O
blood O
in O
distinguishing O
bvFTD O
from O
psychiatric O
disorders. O
Study O
quality O
was O
assessed O
using O
the O
Quality O
Assessment O
Of O
Diagnostic O
Accuracy O
Studies-2 O
tool. O
A O
total O
of O
3828 O
titles O
and O
abstracts O
and O
434 O
full-text O
articles O
were O
reviewed, O
yielding O
12 O
articles O
meeting O
eligibility O
criteria. O
The O
studies O
included O
694 O
unique O
patients O
with O
bvFTD O
and O
1594 O
unique O
patients O
with O
a O
range O
of O
psychiatric O
disorders. O
Four O
studies O
measured O
NfL O
levels O
in O
CSF, O
6 O
in O
blood, O
and O
2 O
in O
both. O
Levels O
of O
NfL O
in O
CSF O
and O
blood O
were O
significantly O
higher O
among O
patients O
with O
bvFTD O
than O
patients O
with O
psychiatric O
disorders. O
In O
receiving O
operator O
characteristic O
curve O
analyses, O
the O
area O
under O
the O
curve O
(AUC) O
for O
NfL O
in O
CSF O
for O
bvFTD O
vs O
psychiatric O
disorders O
ranged O
from O
0.86 O
to O
0.95 O
(sensitivities: O
63%-96%, O
specificities: O
81%-100%). O
The O
AUCs O
for O
NfL O
in O
blood O
ranged O
from O
0.79 O
to O
0.98 O
(sensitivities: O
65%-100%, O
specificities: O
69%-96%). O
The O
findings O
in O
this O
systematic O
review O
indicate O
that O
NfL O
may O
help O
supplement O
clinical O
diagnostic O
evaluations O
in O
differentiating O
bvFTD O
from O
psychiatric O
disorder O
diagnoses. O
Considering O
the O
limitations O
of O
the O
existing O
literature, O
future O
studies O
should O
prospectively O
recruit O
patients O
with O
neuropsychiatric O
symptoms, O
quantify O
symptom O
severity, O
obtain O
NfL O
levels O
in O
real-time O
using O
clinically O
available O
assays, O
consider O
the O
potential O
impact O
of O
patient O
age O
on O
diagnostic O
accuracy, O
establish O
clinically O
relevant O
cutoffs, O
and O
correlate O
NfL O
with O
autopsy-confirmed O
brain O
pathology. O

This O
study O
represents O
a O
first O
successful O
use O
of O
a O
genetic O
biomarker O
to O
select O
potential O
responders O
in O
a O
prospective O
study O
in O
psychiatry. O
Liafensine, O
a O
triple O
reuptake O
inhibitor, O
may O
become O
a O
new O
precision O
medicine O
for O
treatment-resistant O
depression O
(TRD), O
a O
major O
unmet O
medical O
need. O
To O
determine O
whether O
ANK3-positive O
patients O
with O
TRD O
benefit O
from O
a O
1-mg O
and/or O
2-mg O
daily O
oral O
dose O
of O
liafensine, O
compared O
with O
placebo, O
in O
a O
clinical O
trial. O
A O
novel O
pharmacogenomic O
biomarker, O
ANK3, O
was O
discovered O
as O
a O
predictor O
of O
liafensine's O
efficacy O
retrospectively. O
In O
this O
biomarker-guided, O
randomized, O
double-blind, O
placebo-controlled, O
phase O
2b O
clinical O
trial O
conducted O
at O
58 O
sites O
from O
July O
2022 O
through O
March O
2024, O
1967 O
patients O
were O
assessed O
for O
eligibility O
and O
189 O
ANK3-positive O
patients O
with O
TRD O
were O
randomized. O
Key O
exclusion O
criteria O
included O
specified O
disorders, O
concomitant O
medications, O
or O
organ O
dysfunction. O
Investigators, O
patients, O
raters, O
and O
sponsors O
were O
blinded O
to O
ANK3 O
status O
and O
treatment. O
Data O
analysis O
was O
performed O
from O
March O
26 O
to O
April O
23, O
2024. O
Patients O
were O
randomized O
