9.74 O
(95% O
CI, O
2.90-32.73) O
per O
100 O
000 O
people. O
The O
primary O
progressive O
aphasia O
variant O
pooled O
crude O
incidence O
was O
0.52 O
(95% O
CI, O
0.35-0.79) O
per O
100 O
000 O
person-years O
and O
prevalence, O
3.67 O
(95% O
CI, O
3.05-4.43). O
FTD O
incidence O
among O
individuals O
younger O
than O
65 O
years O
was O
1.84 O
(95% O
CI, O
0.79-4.30) O
per O
100 O
000 O
person-years O
and O
prevalence, O
7.47 O
(95% O
CI, O
4.13-13.49) O
per O
100 O
000 O
people. O
The O
denominator O
based O
on O
census O
data O
showed O
less O
heterogeneity O
than O
the O
population O
at O
risk O
defined O
by O
the O
authors O
(I2: O
for O
incidence, O
91.6% O
vs O
97.6%, O
respectively, O
and O
