individuals O
living O
with O
dementia O
and O
care O
partners O
require O
informed O
support O
for O
decision O
making. O
We O
conducted O
an O
umbrella O
review O
to O
assess O
knowledge O
translation O
(KT) O
interventions O
supporting O
decision O
making O
for O
individuals O
living O
with O
dementia O
and O
their O
informal O
care O
partners. O
Four O
databases O
were O
searched O
using O
50 O
different O
search O
terms, O
identifying O
22 O
reviews O
presenting O
32 O
KT O
interventions. O
The O
most O
common O
KT O
decision O
topic O
was O
ACP O
(N O
= O
21) O
which O
includes O
advanced O
care O
directives, O
feeding O
options, O
and O
placement O
in O
long-term O
care. O
The O
majority O
of O
KT O
interventions O
targeted O
care O
partners O
only O
(N O
= O
16), O
or O
both O
care O
partners O
and O
individuals O
living O
with O
dementia O
(N O
= O
13), O
with O
fewer O
interventions O
(N O
= O
3) O
targeting O
individuals O
living O
with O
dementia. O
Overall, O
our O
umbrella O
review O
offers O
insights O
into O
the O
beneficial O
impacts O
of O
KT O
interventions, O
such O
as O
increased O
knowledge O
and O
confidence, O
and O
decreased O
decisional O
conflicts. O
HIGHLIGHTS: O
Knowledge O
translation O
(KT) O
helps O
people O
with O
dementia O
and O
caregivers O
make O
decisions. O
Our O
umbrella O
review O
investigated O
whether O
KT O
interventions O
helped O
decision O
making. O
KT O
interventions O
were O
beneficial, O
with O
advance O
care O
planning O
being O
the O
main O
topic. O
Thirteen O
(41%) O
of O
the O
32 O
KT O
interventions O
were O
found O
to O
be O
freely O
accessible O
online. O
We O
recommend O
the O
creation O
of O
a O
KT O
toolkit O
to O
guide O
topic-specific O
decision O
making. O

Initial O
