modality O
functions O
to O
some O
degree O
as O
a O
relevant O
source O
for O
recognition O
memory. O
Yet O
our O
results O
propose O
that O
familiarity O
is O
more O
strongly O
affected O
than O
recollection O
if O
contextual O
information O
beyond O
dimensionality O
is O
matched O
between O
encoding O
modalities. O

Extensive O
research O
has O
confirmed O
that O
omega-3 O
fatty O
acids O
provide O
